# Console verification (mandatory when touching console)

After editing files matched by this rule, run the **fixed verification pipeline** before claiming the work is done:

```powershell
# Full pipeline: Java unit tests → frontend build → Podman Playwright UI/E2E
.\scripts\verify-console.ps1

# Faster iteration when the container image is already built:
.\scripts\verify-console.ps1 -SkipBuild -KeepContainer
```

## Pipeline phases

| Phase | What | Script / command |
|-------|------|------------------|
| Unit | Console REST, health, static resource, Jackson ID tests | `scripts/verify-console-unit.ps1` |
| Build | `tsc` + Vite production bundle | `npm run build` in `data-generator-console-web` |
| UI/E2E | Playwright specs under `e2e/specs/` against Podman service | `scripts/e2e-podman.ps1` |

## E2E layout

- `e2e/specs/api.*.spec.ts` — REST smoke
- `e2e/specs/navigation.spec.ts`, `home.spec.ts`, `pages.spec.ts` — page coverage
- `e2e/specs/theme.spec.ts`, `acceptance.spec.ts` — dual-theme UI acceptance
- `e2e/specs/template-workflow.spec.ts` — save-template business flow

CI runs the same pipeline on push/PR when console paths change (`.github/workflows/console-verify.yml`).

Do **not** skip verification for console-only bugfixes unless the user explicitly opts out.
